Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Tet10 boundary-conforming fixed-port label route with
 carrier-weighted gates

Label production moves from CGAL Mesh_3 interior + non-nested P1 ports to
Gmsh volume meshes whose port faces are the carrier trace itself, midpoint
refined k times (P exactly nested, dyadic weights, affine error 0), with
Tet10 (straight-sided P2) displacement instead of locked Tet4.

- tet10_label.py: Tet10 promotion with carrier-lifted port midpoints, dense
  fixed-port Schur (SuperLU / MKL Pardiso above 1M internal dof), carrier
  mass + Laplace-Beltrami norms and low-frequency operator comparison.
- conforming_port_mesh.py: carrier shell refinement, polyhedron-preserving
  cavity surface smoothing, Gmsh volume meshing (HXT/Delaunay/Frontal,
  Netgen optimization), watertight and quality reports.
- scripts: run_conforming_port_mesh, run_tet10_label_gates,
  combine_tet10_label_gates, produce_tet10_label (production command with
  per-stratum resolution presets, create-only outputs, SHA-256 receipts).
- CGAL topology gate: nonmanifold_boundary_edge_count becomes a bounded
  field (limit 8) instead of hard-zero; the C++ wrapper reports instead of
  aborting (duplicate boundary facets remain fatal).
- tests: test_tet10_label.py (promotion partition of unity, symmetric PSD
  Schur annihilating rigid modes, constant-strain patch test Tet4 == Tet10,
  carrier norms, nested shell refinement); gate tests updated.
- artifacts/.../tet10_conforming_label_route_v1: ADDENDUM_04 (frozen
  protocol), STEP1/STEP2 reports, six-case panel gates (reproducibility
  0.23-0.37% over Netgen-optimized meshers, convergence 0.65-0.85%),
  cut-position sweep (no operator jump across carrier grid lines),
  2x1x1 assembly validation with constrained-monolithic control, label
  receipts.

